{{!
    @template mod_luminationtutor/message

    One question and the tutor's reply. amd/src/chat.js builds the same markup for a new question.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * id - Message id, 0 while it is being sent.
    * message - The question as typed (escaped here).
    * replyhtml - The reply as HTML, cleaned by format_text().
    * pending - Whether the reply is still being written.
    * failed - Whether the tutor could not answer.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "id": 1,
        "message": "What is photosynthesis?",
        "replyhtml": "<p>It is how plants make food from light.</p>",
        "pending": false,
        "failed": false
    }
}}
<div class="mod_luminationtutor-message mb-2" data-region="message" data-messageid="{{id}}"{{#pending}} data-pending="1"{{/pending}}>
    <div class="mod_luminationtutor-question p-2 mb-1 rounded">{{message}}</div>
    <div class="mod_luminationtutor-reply p-2 rounded" data-region="reply">
        {{#pending}}<span class="text-muted">{{#str}}thinking, mod_luminationtutor{{/str}}</span>{{/pending}}
        {{#failed}}<span class="text-danger">{{#str}}replyfailed, mod_luminationtutor{{/str}}</span>{{/failed}}
        {{{replyhtml}}}
    </div>
</div>
